stage: cfg (amplification / resource consumption)
kind: OOM (libFuzzer rss > 2GB default limit)
site: parse → Cfg::build (no single panic site; allocation blow-up)
repro: cargo fuzz run fuzz_cfg fuzz/crashes/fuzz_cfg/oom-268ac1d3377b
size: 113 bytes

Not a panic — libFuzzer killed the process with exit 71 (OOM) during
the 60s smoke. A 113-byte DEX-shaped input made parse + CFG construction
allocate past 2GiB. Likely amplification via a header field (method_ids_size,
class_defs_size, or code_item registers_size) multiplied by per-entry
allocation.

Filed during dex-hardening's fuzz re-smoke (directive #7). Handed off
to `dex-hardening-sweep` for root-cause analysis: add size sanity bounds
at the parser boundary (reject entity counts > data.len() / sizeof(entry)),
which is the standard defense against DEX amplification. Not in scope
for dex-hardening.
